---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-privy';
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS vs Privy: replacing messaging and capture";
const desc = "Evaluate Privy after Yotpo messaging retirement: rebuild capture, welcome and cart ownership while retaining Reviews and Loyalty deliberately.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Privy capture feeding Yotpo Email?",
    "answer": "Do not design a new handoff to retired Yotpo messaging. Feed a working destination and verify its consent and suppression behavior."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a migration offer guarantee access to my old data?",
    "answer": "No. Confirm which files and assets you already hold and ask Privy what can be migrated from them. The inactive source dashboard is not an assured export route."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I abandon Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty?",
    "answer": "Those are separate decisions. Name the retained product, supported connection and sender for each job. A Loyalty connection does not establish review-request ownership."
  },
  {
    "question": "What decides whether Privy fits?",
    "answer": "Demonstrate your forms, welcome branches, purchase suppression and needed data handoffs. Compare current total cost and operating effort against your own requirements without arbitrary traffic or order thresholds."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="link" href="/compare">← Comparisons</a>
      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Migration decision</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Privy should be evaluated as a possible replacement for messaging and storefront capture, rather than as a popup layer feeding retired Yotpo Email. The useful question is whether your forms, permissions, journeys and retained Yotpo data can reach a working destination without duplicate messages.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Retirement changes the comparison</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/integrations">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a> reports a decommissioned SMS application with inactive dashboard and background services. Do not follow older advice to launch Yotpo Email after Privy capture improves. Build from records and assets already available to your business. Missing historic suppressions or templates need a documented recovery request and fallback, not an assumption of fresh dashboard access.</p>
        <h2>Treat the migration offer as a scoped conversation</h2>
        <p>Privy’s <a href="https://www.privy.com/comparison/yotpo">Yotpo migration page</a> describes email and SMS migration assistance. It also contains a dated promotion. Obtain current scope and terms instead of copying the offer into a budget. Ask which assets the team can use when the source dashboard is unavailable, which journeys require rebuilding, who verifies permissions and who signs off the final trigger map.</p>
        <h2>Inventory every live capture surface</h2>
        <p>List theme popups, landing forms, checkout choices and any agency-managed displays. Record which audience each targets and which system receives the submission. A form that still renders may lead nowhere. Replace or disable abandoned endpoints, remove duplicate displays and preserve the disclosure associated with each channel. A higher signup count is not enough if it loses source attribution, discount conditions or separate SMS permission.</p>
        <h2>The popup-to-welcome handoff</h2>
        <p>Proposed acceptance exercise: sign up as a new email subscriber, a returning subscriber, an existing purchaser and a suppressed address. Check the expected welcome branch and verify that a repeat submission does not restart an inappropriate discount sequence. If another ESP remains the email owner, prove the handoff there and disable the competing welcome in Privy. If Privy owns email, remove the stale external destination rather than leaving two apparent owners.</p>
        <h2>Cart recovery must stop on purchase</h2>
        <p>Build a small case register covering a completed purchase, a cancelled order, a changed cart and a shared customer record. Confirm that recovery does not continue merely because the initial capture event was valid. For made-to-order products, explain production expectations instead of adding false urgency. For a gift order, avoid assuming the purchaser wants replenishment. Keep transactional order messages separate from promotional recovery.</p>
        <h2>Keep Reviews and Loyalty explicit</h2>
        <p>Retaining Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty does not mean retaining Yotpo Email & SMS. Privy’s <a href="https://www.privy.com/changelog">changelog</a> describes bringing Yotpo loyalty data into Privy for segmentation and Flows. Confirm account availability, fields and update behavior before depending on it. Review collection still needs a named sender and exclusion rules. Do not infer that a Loyalty field supplies review status, permission or shared message suppression.</p>
        <h2>Choose a useful capture experiment</h2>
        <p>Compare forms against your own traffic mix and offer economics. Keep the audience and reporting window identifiable, and record both eligible signups and resulting unsubscribes or support issues. A product-preview incentive for print-on-demand shoppers and a restock alert for existing customers serve different purposes. There is no universal capture-rate threshold that makes Privy mandatory, and no order-count ceiling that proves a store must leave it.</p>
        <h2>Reconcile cost and release responsibility</h2>
        <p>Ask for current pricing at your projected billable audience and sending volume, plus SMS usage and migration work. Include any retained review, loyalty or separate email tools. Before release, assign the person who can change a form, pause a journey, answer replies and reconcile suppressions. A marketer should rehearse those actions on the actual intended setup. Record what passed and what remains incomplete; do not turn a proposed rehearsal into a claimed conversion lift.</p>
      </article>
      <nav class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4" aria-label="Related guides">
        <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-privy">Omnisend and Privy</a>
        <a class="link" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">Welcome series</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
